Take an interface back from olr.

Nothing on the interface is undone — releasing does not remove an address
or stop a daemon. What it removes is permission, so any address range,
resolver or exit still naming this interface will be refused the next
time it is applied. Remove those first if you mean to stop serving on it.

Usage:
  olr release <interface> [flags]

Flags:
  -h, --help   help for release

Global Flags:
      --dry-run         show what would change and exit without applying it
  -o, --output string   output format: text|json (default "text")
      --socket string   olrd control socket (default "/run/olr/olrd.sock")
